---
title: Loudness metering (LUFS)
description: Measure loudness in LUFS with Splitwave's EBU R128 meter and check streams, podcasts and broadcasts against Spotify, Apple, ACX and ATSC targets.
order: 1
---

Peak meters tell you whether audio clips; **loudness meters** tell you how loud it *sounds*. Streaming services and broadcasters normalise by loudness, measured in **LUFS** (LKFS in the US), so hitting their target keeps your audio from being turned down or sounding quiet next to others.

## What the meter shows

| Reading | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| M (Momentary) | Loudness over the last 400 ms. Reacts fast. |
| S (Short-term) | Loudness over the last 3 s. Good for riding levels. |
| I (Integrated) | Loudness of everything since the last reset. This is the number targets refer to. |
| True Peak | The highest peak between samples, in dBTP. |
| Loudness Range | How much the loudness varies over time, in LU. |
| Peak / Loudness | Difference between true peak and integrated loudness. |
| RMS and Floor | Average level and the noise floor, used by ACX checks. |

Click **Reset peaks** to start a new measurement.

## Delivery profiles

Pick a profile and the meter checks your audio against it, with a green or red mark per requirement.

| Profile | Integrated | True peak |
| --- | --- | --- |
| EBU R128 | -23 LUFS | -1 dBTP |
| ITU-R BS.1770 | -23 LUFS | -1 dBTP |
| ATSC A/85 | -24 LKFS | -2 dBTP |
| AES TD1008 | -16 LUFS | -1 dBTP |
| Apple | -16 LUFS | -1 dBTP |
| Spotify | -14 LUFS | -1 dBTP |
| ACX (audiobooks) | RMS -23 to -18 dB, peak -3 dB, floor -60 dB | |

Integrated loudness passes when it is within 1 LU of the target.

## Hitting a target

1. Put the Loudness meter last, after your [Limiter](/wiki/effects/limiter).
2. Play a representative section and watch **I** settle.
3. Raise or lower the level before the limiter (Gain or the Compressor's makeup) until **I** reaches the target.
4. Set the limiter's ceiling at or below the profile's true peak.
